This product is a modified version of tiny-voca
(https://github.com/n4ze3m/tiny-voca), Copyright Muhammed Nazeem,
licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

Main changes from tiny-voca:
- Hebrew text front end: RenikudPlus G2P (default) or phonikud, a Hebrew
  phoneme inventory with stress marks, Hebrew number reading and sentence
  splitting.
- One voice ("AH") instead of two English voices.
- Forced alignment settings for Hebrew, a parallel data preparation script and
  the recital-v3 data recipe (ivrit.ai crowd-recital, voice-converted with
  kNN-VC).
- RunPod training scripts, ONNX export metadata for the Hebrew front end, and a
  Hebrew browser demo.

Third-party components used at run time or in the data recipe:
- RenikudPlus (https://github.com/maxmelichov/RenikudPlus), Apache-2.0.
- kNN-VC (https://github.com/bshall/knn-vc), MIT.
- ONNX Runtime Web (https://onnxruntime.ai), MIT.
- wav2vec2 phoneme recogniser facebook/wav2vec2-lv-60-espeak-cv-ft
  (forced alignment), Apache-2.0.

The released he-v3 weights (models/he-v3) were trained on audio derived from
ivrit.ai's crowd-recital dataset (https://huggingface.co/datasets/ivrit-ai/crowd-recital),
used under the ivrit.ai License v2. Credit: ivrit.ai. See models/he-v3/LICENSE.
